The site development plans for a subdivision shall be clearly and legibly drawn at a scale of not less than 100 feet to one inch. The sheet size shall not exceed 36 inches by 48 inches, and the minimum sheet size shall be 17 inches by 22 inches, The site development plans shall include the following information:
(1) Name of subdivision;
(2) Name, address and telephone numbers of the owner/developer of the property;
(3) Name, address and telephone number of the professional engineer who prepared the plans;
(4) Name, address and telephone number of the designated 24-hour contact person for the project;
(5) Date plans were prepared, north arrow and graphic scale on all appropriate sheets;
(6) Location map at a scale of 600 feet to one inch;
(7) An accurate list of conditions relative to the zoning of the property and the approval of the concept plat and preliminary plat;
(8) Pertinent site development data;
(9) Detailed limits of clearing;
(10) Tree protection and landscape plans;
(11) Detailed erosion and sediment control plans;
(12) Detailed grading and drainage plans;
(13) Reserved;
(14) Detailed roadway plans;
(15) Detailed storm sewer plans;
(16) Detailed water utility plans;
(17) Detailed sanitary sewer plans;
